h the  4th 1896 while dynamite dick clifton and  little dick west were gunned down in  1897 and 1898 respectively we're left  with just one man bill doolin the leader  of the wild bunch in june 1896 guardsman  bill tillman captured him without  incident at eureka springs arkansas and  sent him to federal prison in guthrie  oklahoma to await trial as it happened  clifton was also in prison there so the  two of them and a dozen other inmates  executed a prison break on july the 5th  doolin ran away to his father-in-law's  farm in lawson oklahoma to be with his  wife and son perhaps he realized that it  was the end of the road for him so he  wanted one more chance to see his family  unsurprisingly marshall soon tracked him  down to the homestead on august 25 1896  they trapped doolin in an ambush like  dalton he could have surrendered but he  preferred to go out shooting so doolin  raised his gun and aimed it at the  marshals but didn't get a chance to pull  the trigger before one of the deputies  emptied a double-barreled shotgun  straight into his chest and then there  were none eleven violent deaths for  eleven violent men meant the end of the  most ruthless gang that the old west had  ever seen the gang known  as the wild bunch i hope you found  today's video interesting if you did  please do hit that like button below  don't forget to subscribe and thank you  for watching  [Music]
 

